# Goal: no dump, log or firmware gets in by accident, while the legitimate
# files of a port (docs, scripts, device packaging) stay visible. Broad rules
# come first; the re-includes for legitimate files are at the END of this file.
# Note: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is ignored.
#
# Objetivo: que ningún volcado, log o firmware entre por accidente, sin ocultar
# los ficheros legítimos del port. Las reglas amplias van primero; las
# re-inclusiones de lo legítimo, al FINAL del fichero.

# ==== Private data: never commit ====
# Typical dump directories are ignored entirely, at any depth.
backups/
backup/
private/
secrets/
dumps/
dump/
tmp/
/scratch/

# ==== Logs and diagnostics (may contain serial, IMEI, MAC, accounts) ====
# Any file or directory whose name contains these words, at any depth and with
# any extension. Docs and scripts with these words are re-included at the end.
# The most critical ones are case-insensitive.
*[gG][eE][tT][vV][aA][rR]*
*[gG][eE][tT][pP][rR][oO][pP]*
*[dD][mM][eE][sS][gG]*
*[lL][oO][gG][cC][aA][tT]*
*[dD][uU][mM][pP][sS][tT][aA][tT][eE]*
*[bB][uU][gG][rR][eE][pP][oO][rR][tT]*
*[pP][sS][tT][oO][rR][eE]*
*[rR][aA][mM][oO][oO][pP][sS]*
*[kK][mM][sS][gG]*
*[tT][oO][mM][bB][sS][tT][oO][nN][eE]*
*adb-devices*
*udevadm*
uevent
devices.txt
*.[lL][oO][gG]
logs/
*.trace
*.out

